---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<Layout title="Privacy policy" description="How Tarian Ventures Limited handles website visits, enquiries and professional outreach, including your privacy rights.">
  <PageIntro label="Legal information" title="Privacy policy"><p>How we handle your personal information.</p></PageIntro>
  <div class="shell legal-content">
    <p>Last updated: 1 October 2026</p>
    <aside class="review-notice" aria-label="Review status"><strong>Pre-launch review</strong><p>The business practices below have been confirmed. Provider processing locations, transfer safeguards, backup retention and website logging remain to be verified before this notice is published.</p></aside>
    <section><h2>Who we are</h2><p>{site.company.registeredName}, registered in {site.company.jurisdiction} with company number {site.company.number}, is the controller responsible for the personal information described here. Our registered office is {site.company.registeredOffice}.</p><p>This policy covers our website, enquiries and early-stage business conversations, including Tarian Compute and AltGRC. It does not cover future product services, customer deployments or separate venture companies, which will need their own privacy information.</p><p>Dan Winder handles privacy questions, requests and complaints. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.general}`}>{site.contact.general}</a> or write to our registered office.</p></section>
    <section><h2>What we collect and where it comes from</h2><p>When you contact us, we receive the information you provide, such as your name, business email address, organisation, role, telephone number, message and attachments. We may record correspondence and relevant notes to follow up the conversation.</p><p>For professional outreach, we may obtain names, roles, business contact details and relevant professional information from company websites, public LinkedIn profiles, introductions and existing professional contacts. We do not buy contact lists. We provide this notice at our first contact and, where required, within one month of obtaining your information.</p><p>Our hosting services receive technical information needed to deliver and protect the website, such as IP addresses and requested pages. The website has no contact form, account registration, analytics, advertising trackers or embedded media. Email links open your own email application. See our <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.</p><p>Please only send information relevant to your enquiry and avoid unnecessary sensitive information or details about other people.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Why we use information</h2><p>We use information to answer enquiries, follow up relevant conversations and assess business opportunities. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests: developing Tarian's activities and establishing relevant professional relationships, balanced against your rights and reasonable expectations.</p><p>Our initial unsolicited outreach is limited to individually selected contacts at UK limited companies and other incorporated organisations, using their business contact details. We do not run newsletters, automated campaigns or bulk mailings. Public availability of contact information does not by itself justify contacting someone; the message must be relevant to their professional role.</p><p>If you personally ask us to take steps towards a contract with you, the lawful basis may instead be those pre-contractual steps or performance of that contract. This does not automatically apply when you represent a company. We may also process information to meet a specific legal obligation.</p><p>You are not obliged to provide enquiry information, but without sufficient details we may be unable to answer or progress your request.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Your choice about outreach</h2><p>You can object to direct marketing at any time by replying to a message or emailing our privacy contact. We will stop that outreach. Our messages include a simple way to decline further contact.</p><p>We keep only the minimum contact details and objection record needed on a local do-not-contact list to prevent further outreach. We retain that record for as long as needed to honour your preference and review its necessity periodically. It is not used for marketing.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Who has access and how we store information</h2><p>Dan Winder is the only person within Tarian who accesses the enquiry mailboxes and records. IONOS provides our email service. Email copies are downloaded to Apple Mail on a secure local machine, and relevant enquiry details may be kept in a local spreadsheet.</p><p>We do not enter enquiry information into AI tools, a cloud CRM or a mailing list, or share it with prospective partners. We do not sell personal information.</p><p>Microsoft Azure Static Web Apps hosts the website. Cloudflare is our domain registrar. Service providers process the information necessary to supply their services; this is separate from access to our local enquiry records. We may disclose information where legally required.</p><p>We limit records to what is needed for the relevant purpose and restrict local access. No method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed completely secure.</p></section>
    <section><h2>How long we keep information</h2><ul><li>Closed enquiries that lead to no further work: deleted within 12 months of the last substantive contact, unless a specific continuing need is documented.</li><li>Unanswered outreach: deleted within 12 months of our last outreach, apart from the minimal do-not-contact record described above.</li><li>Active business relationships: reviewed annually, with information deleted when no longer needed. Relevant records may be kept for an ongoing business, contractual or legal reason.</li><li>Privacy requests and complaints: retained only as needed to handle the matter and demonstrate the response or meet a continuing legal need, with necessity reviewed annually.</li></ul><p>Deletion covers the live IONOS mailbox, local Apple Mail copies and spreadsheet entries. Where information must be retained for a legal obligation or dispute, the reason is recorded and retention limited to that need.</p><p>IONOS also maintains backups. Removing a message from a live mailbox does not establish that every backup copy has immediately been erased. The applicable backup lifecycle and any separate email-archiving service must be confirmed before launch.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Provider processing and international transfers</h2><p>Local enquiry records are held on our secure local machine. Email and website delivery also involve our service providers; we do not claim that all their processing takes place in the UK.</p><p>The service-specific processing locations, any restricted international transfers and applicable safeguards are being checked before publication. This section will identify the confirmed arrangements and how to obtain details of the safeguards. Website log retention will also be specified once the deployed configuration has been checked.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Depending on the circumstances, you may ask to access your information, correct it, erase it, restrict its use or receive a portable copy. You can object to processing based on legitimate interests, and your right to object to direct marketing is absolute. Where consent is the basis for processing, you may withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p><p>Contact Dan using the details above. We normally respond without undue delay and within one month. Requests are normally free; lawful exceptions or extensions may apply, and we will explain them. We may ask for proportionate information to verify your identity.</p><p>We do not use your information for profiling or solely automated decisions with legal or similarly significant effects.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Complaints</h2><p>Please contact us if you are concerned about our use of your information. We will acknowledge a privacy complaint within 30 days, investigate without undue delay, keep you informed and explain the outcome.</p><p>You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office, the UK data protection regulator, through the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ICO complaints service</a>.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We will update this policy when our activities or arrangements change and show the revised date. We will provide further privacy information before using personal information for a new purpose where required.</p></section>
  </div>
</Layout>
